WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.688
Let’s walk through Population Sentiments.

00:00:02.688 --> 00:00:06.700
Read the published sentiment as audience-specific scenario context.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.700
Identify who received it, what changed in the narrative

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.575
, and whether the team will respond;

00:00:11.575 --> 00:00:14.475
do not treat sentiment as a hidden score or automatic

00:00:14.475 --> 00:00:15.588
outcome.

00:00:15.588 --> 00:00:18.887
On this slide, read White Cell-published sentiment updates for

00:00:18.887 --> 00:00:19.887
the team.

00:00:19.887 --> 00:00:23.300
In practice, decide explicitly whether and how the published

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.562
narrative changes the next action.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:29.335
When you are ready, use Open Population Sentiments to

00:00:29.335 --> 00:00:31.273
move to the live surface.

00:00:31.273 --> 00:00:34.060
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:34.210
.
